#: includes/views/settings.php:78
msgid "Each site keeps its media in its own folder, so several sites can share one storage. The media keep their year/month structure inside it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:85
msgid "Transfer and serving"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:89
msgid "How files are served"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:94
msgid "Transparent proxy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:96
msgid "Addresses stay exactly as they were (/wp-content/uploads/…). A small PHP script without WordPress streams each missing file from the storage. Every request that is not cached takes a PHP process and traffic of the site hosting, so it works best behind Cloudflare or another CDN."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:99
msgid "Directly from the storage"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:101
msgid "Pages link straight to the storage (or your subdomain of it) and old addresses are redirected there. The fastest option: the site does no work for media at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:103
msgid "The mode can be switched at any time; files do not move."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:107
msgid "Verification"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:109
msgid "Strict: download every copy from its public address and compare its SHA-256 with the local file"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:110
msgid "Without it, the size in the storage and the size served at the public address are compared. Local files are deleted only after verification in both modes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:116
msgid "Move new uploads to the storage automatically after everything has been moved"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:117
msgid "A few minutes after an upload, once WordPress has created the thumbnails, the new files are copied, verified and deleted locally. If the storage is unavailable they stay in WordPress."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:121
msgid "Redirect for old addresses"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:124
msgid "302 — temporary (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:125
msgid "301 — permanent"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:127
msgid "Only for the \"Directly from the storage\" mode: pages link to the storage, and the redirect catches old /wp-content/uploads/ links. Browsers remember a 301 for a long time, which breaks images for those visitors after the files are returned to WordPress."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:136
msgid "Connection test"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:137
msgid "Uploads a small file to the site folder, reads it back through the public address and deletes it. Real media are not touched."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:138
msgid "Test the connection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:141
msgid "Preparing the storage"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:143
msgid "In the hosting control panel, open the storage and the \"Users and API\" tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:144
msgid "Add a user with the Read, Write and Content rights and enter its login and password here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:145
msgid "For the \"Public access\" user, enable only \"Read\": files open by direct links while the file list stays hidden."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/settings.php:146
msgid "Optionally, on the \"Settings\" tab of the storage, set browser caching and the HTTP to HTTPS redirect, and connect your own subdomain for the public address."
msgstr ""
